              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 291,
                "quote": "WrittenOff = payment.WrittenOff > 0m"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The new rules sit in Tier 2: the allocation oldest first in Accounts.allocate, the write-off in Payments.pay, and the threshold in Policy.writeOffBelow. The change also moves the borrow block out of the CLI, which is an improvement. However, the decision to refuse a blocked borrow is now made in the Tier 3 use case, not inside Loans.borrow, so a Tier 3 site is still enforcing a domain rule. The Tier 3 view also re-derives the write-off flag with a local predicate (WrittenOff > 0m). Both agree with Tier 2, so this is a partial duplication, not a contradiction.",
            "score": 1
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The change adds no effects. Allocation, settlement and write-off are pure functions in Tier 2. The CLI no longer calls ports.Store.Load() for the borrow rule, which reduces Tier 4 re-entry. The JSON codec change is confined to the existing Tier 4 persistence adapter.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The write-off threshold is defined once, as Policy.writeOffBelow. The blocking balance literal 5.00m is removed from the CLI, so Policy.blockingBalance is now the only definition. The new Accounts.owed formula includes WrittenOff and is the single definition used by the views, Payments.pay and isBlocked. No fact is restated.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "All waiver rules are in Tier 2: approver required, the earliest fine for the copy with something unpaid, the waived amount equal to the unpaid part, and the Waived standing in Accounts.allocate. UseCases.waive only calls Waivers.waive. The views and the CLI only format the standing as text. The `paid = 0m` branch in Views only chooses between two wordings and does not re-decide any rule.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "Waivers.waive is pure, and its result is persisted by the existing commit path through the Store port. No clock, I/O or console use is added below Tier 4. The codec change is in the Tier 4 persistence adapter. The CLI only parses the command and renders a Tier 3 view.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "Fines.waivedOf is the single definition of what a waiver took off a fine. Accounts.owed, Accounts.allocate and Fines.outstanding all call it, so the three amount calculations cannot drift apart. The paid portion of a waived fine is stored once, as Waived, and derived from it as Amount - Waived. The error texts and the help line are each defined once.",
            "score": 2
          }
        }
